# Runtime Container Verification

Use these commands from the operator shell to validate the real runtime context
after cutover.

## Runtime Container

- container: `{{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }}`
- bridge URL: `{{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_url }}`
- recovery URL: `{{ openclaw_runtime_recovery_url }}`
- bridge auth env: `{{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_auth_env }}`

## Reachability

- Bridge health from inside the runtime container:
  - `docker exec {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }} sh -lc 'curl -fsS {{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_url }}/healthz'`
- Recovery health from inside the runtime container:
  - `docker exec {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }} sh -lc 'curl -fsS {{ openclaw_runtime_recovery_url }}/healthz'`
- Name resolution from inside the runtime container:
  - `docker exec {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }} sh -lc 'getent hosts {{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_host }} || ping -c 1 {{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_host }}'`

## Real Bridge Operation

- Confirm the bridge auth token env exists:
  - `docker exec {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }} sh -lc 'test -n "${{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_auth_env }}"; echo $?'`
- Run a real bridge operation through `/v1/bridge`:
  - `docker exec {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }} sh -lc 'curl -fsS -X POST {{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_url }}/v1/bridge -H "content-type: application/json" -H "authorization: Bearer ${{ "{" }}{{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_auth_env }}{{ "}" }}" --data "{\"operation\":\"health.check\",\"arguments\":{}}"'`

## Recovery Operation

- Run an authenticated recovery self-heal request:
  - `docker exec {{ openclaw_legacy_runtime_container_name }} sh -lc 'curl -fsS -X POST {{ openclaw_runtime_recovery_url }}/v1/self-heal -H "content-type: application/json" -H "authorization: Bearer ${{ "{" }}{{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_auth_env }}{{ "}" }}" --data "{}"'`

## Pass Rule

Post-cutover runtime verification is green only if:

- the runtime container resolves `{{ openclaw_runtime_bridge_host }}`
- both `/healthz` endpoints answer from inside the runtime container
- the real `health.check` bridge operation succeeds with auth
- the recovery endpoint accepts an authenticated request
